      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(tts): validate maxLength is a positive finite number",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`setTtsMaxLength` accepts any number value without validation. Negative, NaN, Infinity, or zero values can be persisted to disk, causing downstream TTS failures when these invalid values are used as speech length limits.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe function writes directly to user preference files on disk. Adding an input guard prevents corruption of persisted settings and produces an immediate, clear error instead of a delayed crash.\n\n## User Impact\n\nInvalid maxLength values are rejected at the API boundary with a descriptive RangeError, preventing silent misconfiguration of TTS speech length limits.\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- [x] This change is backwards compatible\n- [x] This change has been tested with existing configurations\n",
        "branch": "fix/tts-maxlength-validation",
